  "ingredients": [
    "1 1/2 cup almond flour",
    "1 teaspoon dried oregano",
    "1/4 teaspoon salt",
    "1/4 cup olive oil (plus extra if needed)",
    "6 ounce bacon",
    "1 medium green bell pepper",
    "1 teaspoon fresh garlic",
    "6 large egg",
    "1 1/2 cup cheddar cheese (grated)",
    "1 teaspoon all-purpose seasoning (such as Mrs. Dash)",
    "1/2 teaspoon black pepper",
    "1/4 teaspoon salt"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 350F. Cut the bacon into chunks and place them in a pan to cook.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the bacon is cooking, add the almond flour, oregano, and salt to a mixing bowl.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the olive oil to the dough and mix it in.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roll the dough into a ball. If needed, add a little bit more olive oil to help get the consistency right.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spread the dough out into a casserole dish, making it as even as possible.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 20 minutes. The dough won't be fully cooked yet — just enough for it to stick together. The dough will continue cooking after adding the egg filling.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove the bacon from the pan and set on a paper towel to cool. Reserve the bacon grease for later.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dice the green pepper and mince the garlic.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-09.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the bell pepper and garlic to the bacon fat to cook.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-08.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Crack the eggs into a measuring cup and whisk them together until well combined.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the bacon, cheddar cheese, green peppers, garlic, reserved bacon fat, Mrs. Dash Table Blend, pepper, and salt. Mix until fully combined.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-11.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour the bacon and egg mixture into the crust and spread it out evenly.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-12.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 15–18 minutes or until the center is firm. Optional: Broil for 3–5 minutes to get a golden brown crust.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/almond-crusted-keto-quiche-13.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove from the oven, let cool, and cut into slices. The first piece usually is the piece I have to \"ruin\" because the crust gets a bit messed up. Use a silicone spatula to remove the rest of the slices. Serve and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/almond-crusted-keto-quiche/#wprm-recipe-50849-step-0-13",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
